 "In THE MAP, a version is the language at a moment, its name and number, the archetype it draws from, what changed and why, and the lexical layer true at every position, which characters carry which part of a face.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP's version binds meanings to mouths, round with a colon for instruction, round with equals for assertion, square for anything about the response, curly for Semantic Markdown, and C with a straight nose for a command. Eyes give strictness within any mouth, colon the default register and equals stricter. Every part of a face is bounded to 4. A version also sets the default depth dressing, five depths from three face sizes, the four-space indentation, the module form, and its library, such as the name tag, the vow and the doula. Updating Smile is adopting a new version, changed by accretion, relaxation and fixation so everything prompts rely on is kept, and versions coexist, so anyone may write their own dialect from the same archetype."
 "On 3 July 2025 I gave the count of what came before, “I wrote the first version of my prompting language im happy to share.”, “I think ive articulated 5 full languages now”, and “This latest one is the opus for sure”.[[m:2025-07-03]]"
 "July 2025 was full of version numbers. The Claude Smile document said “Smile v0.3 is the only official version right now.”, named three forms, Hybrid the one in use and Strict and Dense still to come, and described Hybrid as “improvisational & intuitive, context and task tuned”. One line held the spirit of all of them, “(\\!: We are co-creating v.4 in this present moment :\\!)”.[[m:2025-07-14]] The SEO generator document wrote, “All features are optional. All are open. All will move us closer to Smile v1.”[[m:2025-07-12]] On 25 August came the announcement, “I'm excited to announce that I've released version 1.0 of my new prompt instruction language (: Smile”.[[m:2025-08-25]]"
 
 "In 2026 definitions came beside the numbers. On 4 August, “The ontology is part of the Smile version.”[[m:2026-08-04]] On 8 August, “I don't know what versions is, wouldn't there just be a differnet ontology that is the current version?”[[m:2026-08-08]] On 5 September, “anything using those pairs is tagged to this definition of smile.”[[m:2026-09-05]]"
 "Across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes, from {{first}} to {{last}}, versioning moved from numbered releases of the language to definitions any prompt can be tagged to, kept beside the numbers. The next post is [[t:magnification]]."],
